{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMaxLength","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMaxLength","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Coxeter.Length","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.SymmetricCoxeter"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMaxLength.subgroup_finset_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMaxLength.subgroup_finset_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMaxLength.lean#L71-L75","doc":"A subgroup's underlying `Finset` is nonempty — it contains `1`. This is the instance the Young\nsubgroup needs to feed the above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMaxLength.le_len_maxLenElt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMaxLength.le_len_maxLenElt","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMaxLength.lean#L66-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMaxLength.maxLenElt_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMaxLength.maxLenElt_mem","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMaxLength.lean#L62-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMaxLength.maxLenElt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMaxLength.maxLenElt","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMaxLength.lean#L56-L60","doc":"**A choice of maximal-length element.** Noncomputable, and deliberately *a* choice rather than\n*the* longest element: uniqueness is not proved here and `Triangular` does not need it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMaxLength.exists_maxLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMaxLength.exists_maxLength","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMaxLength.lean#L45-L54","doc":"**A maximal-length element exists** in any nonempty finite set of permutations.\n\nElementary — a maximiser of an `ℕ`-valued function on a nonempty `Finset`. It is the existence half\nof \"the longest element of `S_λ`\"; uniqueness is a separate, genuinely harder statement and is not\nclaimed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMaxLength.len","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMaxLength.len","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMaxLength.lean#L41-L43","doc":"The Coxeter length of a permutation, in the type-`A` system used by the `T_w` basis. ","signatureChunk":0}]}